<title>DUBAI: Emirates Bank International group 96 profits up.</title>
<headline>Emirates Bank International group 96 profits up.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(in millions of UAE dirhams)</p>
<p> Group profit				382.28   vs    318.29</p>
<p> Profit available for appropriation  445.36   vs    377.13</p>
<p> Share of associate's profits	    6.86   vs	8.02</p>
<p> Pre-tax				     384.88   vs    323.05</p>
<p> Net interest income		     494.60   vs    443.73</p>
<p> Other income				183.35   vs    177.35</p>
<p> Provisions, other expenses	     54.82   vs     86.31</p>
<p> Proposed total dividend		  94.05   vs     90.05</p>
<p>Full Name: Emirates Bank International PJSC (EBI).</p>
<p>NOTE - The Dubai government owns 80 percent of EBI. The rest is held by about 750 private investors.</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom +9714-626990</p>
</text>
